  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Propylformate may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Propylformate to Histone H1.0, which is then targeted by a complex involving methyl (2S,3R,6R,13S,17S)-3-[(E)-3,4-dimethylpent-2-enoyl]oxy-15,16-dihydroxy-9,13-dimethyl-4,11-dioxo-10-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-5,18-dioxapentacyclo[12.5.0.01,6.02,17.08,13]nonadec-9-ene-17-carboxylate, which ultimately targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The second and third pathways indicate that Propylformate also interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is targeted by two different compounds, both of which in turn target Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings suggest that Propylformate may exert its effects on Phosphodiesterase 6C through distinct molecular mechanisms, possibly involving epigenetic regulation or other biochemical interactions. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, as the specific molecular mechanisms are not fully elucidated."
